--- B. the twelve observations, on tower-http 0.7.1 ---
  CHECK A status=200 OK headers={content-length=2, content-type=text/plain; charset=utf-8}
  CHECK Q1 status=405 Method Not Allowed headers={allow=GET,HEAD, content-length=0}
  CHECK Q2-get status=200 OK headers={content-length=2, content-type=text/plain; charset=utf-8, vary=origin}
  CHECK Q2-options status=200 OK headers={allow=GET,HEAD, content-length=0, vary=origin}
  CHECK Q3-get status=200 OK headers={content-length=2, content-type=text/plain; charset=utf-8, vary=origin}
  CHECK Q3-options status=200 OK headers={access-control-allow-headers=*, access-control-allow-methods=*, allow=GET,HEAD, content-length=0, vary=origin}
  CHECK C status=200 OK headers={access-control-allow-origin=https://app.example, content-length=2, content-type=text/plain; charset=utf-8, vary=origin}
  CHECK D status=200 OK headers={content-length=2, content-type=text/plain; charset=utf-8, vary=origin}
  CHECK E status=200 OK headers={access-control-allow-headers=*, access-control-allow-methods=*, access-control-allow-origin=https://app.example, access-control-max-age=600, allow=GET,HEAD, content-length=0, vary=origin}
  CHECK R1 status=200 OK handler_hits=0
  CHECK P2 status=200 OK headers={access-control-allow-headers=*, access-control-allow-methods=*, access-control-allow-origin=https://app.example, vary=origin}
  CHECK P3 status=404 Not Found headers={}
  CHECK H parse_is_err=true
ASSERT ok   criterion 1: with the allowlist empty the response carries neither access-control-allow-origin nor vary — the router is observably the one a build with no CORS code produces
ASSERT ok   criterion 2: with the allowlist empty an OPTIONS preflight on a GET-only route is still 405 Method Not Allowed
ASSERT ok   unconditional install, bare CorsLayer::new(): every response gains vary: origin, which criterion 1 forbids
ASSERT ok   unconditional install, bare CorsLayer::new(): OPTIONS on a GET-only route becomes 200, not 405, which criterion 2 forbids
ASSERT ok   unconditional install configured with py's literal empty list: every response still gains vary: origin
ASSERT ok   unconditional install configured with py's literal empty list: OPTIONS becomes 200 and even advertises allow-headers and allow-methods, so an empty allowlist is not observationally equivalent to no layer
ASSERT ok   criterion 3: with the allowlist configured, a GET from the allowed origin has that origin echoed back
ASSERT ok   criterion 4: with the allowlist configured, a GET from a different origin receives no access-control-allow-origin
ASSERT ok   criterion 5, and the report gap this run closes: .max_age(Duration::from_secs(600)) compiles and emits access-control-max-age: 600, matching Starlette's always-emitted 600 s default
ASSERT ok   criterion 5 again, from the handler's side: a preflight short-circuits before the inner service runs — the constraint R75 must order around
ASSERT ok   Router::layer answers a preflight for a path no route matches, which is what a preflight needs
ASSERT ok   Router::route_layer does not, returning a bare 404 — so .layer(), not .route_layer(), is the right call
ASSERT ok   criterion 6: a syntactically invalid origin fails at HeaderValue parsing, so it fails while the router is built rather than at request time

